Package: cellular-settings
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pkexec, polkitd
Recommends: modemmanager, network-manager
Description: Network mode, network preference and mobile data of the modem
 A GTK 4 and libadwaita window for what the desktop's settings leave out for
 the cellular modem: the technologies the modem may use, 4G and 5G alone
 among them; how the modem asks the network for service (the EPS UE mode of
 operation, "EPS only, data-centric" on a network without a circuit-switched
 domain); the last reason the network gave for a refusal; and the mobile data
 connections with their access point. The choice can be kept for the next
 boot: the helper of the package writes /etc/diting/modem-mode, which
 diting-modem-setup reads, as root through pkexec.
